  "instance_name": "cultural_stereotype_of_grief",
  "label": "Cultural Stereotype of Grief",
  "description": "The image of a man screaming in a ruined environment is often used in media and memes to represent extreme grief or trauma. This is a cultural trope — a visual shorthand for suffering — that relies on external knowledge of how grief is commonly portrayed in film, television, and internet culture. The meme uses this trope to amplify the emotional impact of the text.",
